    "prompt": "Find an antiderivative: $$\\int \\frac{2x-9\\sqrt x+9}{(x-3\\sqrt x)^{1/3}}\\,dx$$",
    "image": null,
    "choices": null,
    "answer": "$\\frac65\\left(x-3\\sqrt x\\right)^{5/3}+C$",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Solution",
        "body": "Let $u=x-3\\sqrt x$, $du=\\frac{2\\sqrt x-3}{2\\sqrt x}dx$. Since $2x-9\\sqrt x+9=(2\\sqrt x-3)(\\sqrt x-3)$, the integrand times $dx$ is $\\frac{2\\sqrt x(\\sqrt x-3)}{u^{1/3}}du=2u^{2/3}du$, giving $\\frac65u^{5/3}+C$."
      }
    ],
