        "body": "$\\frac1{\\sin^3x\\cos^2x}=\\frac{\\sin^2x+\\cos^2x}{\\sin^3x\\cos^2x}=\\frac1{\\sin x\\cos^2x}+\\frac1{\\sin^3x}$, and $\\frac1{\\sin x\\cos^2x}=\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2x}+\\frac1{\\sin x}$. Use $\\int\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2x}dx=\\sec x$, $\\int\\csc x\\,dx=\\ln|\\tan\\frac x2|$ and $\\int\\csc^3x\\,dx=-\\frac12\\csc x\\cot x+\\frac12\\ln|\\tan\\frac x2|$. (Differentiating the result confirms it.)"
      }
